<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sobibor extermination camp</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1942–1943</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sobibór</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sobibor was a Nazi extermination camp in eastern German-occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, built as part of Operation Reinhard. From May 1942 to October 1943 some 170,000 to 250,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> were murdered there in gas chambers. On 14 October 1943 prisoners led by Alexander Pechersky and Leon Feldhendler rose up and about 300 escaped, after which the Germans closed and demolished the camp.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sobibor-extermination-camp.jpg" alt="Sobibor extermination camp" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sobibor_extermination_camp_view,_summer_1943_(retouched).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
